WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.399 --> 00:00:04.399
Hey Lisa, what are we going to go do?

00:00:04.399 --> 00:00:06.170
We’re going to go, vote!

00:00:06.170 --> 00:00:09.130
We’re going to vote.

00:00:09.130 --> 00:00:10.599
We marching.

00:00:10.599 --> 00:00:15.039
Goes on and on and on.

00:00:15.039 --> 00:00:17.119
The line stretched outside of the school.

00:00:17.119 --> 00:00:21.980
Millions of people mailing in their ballots
and finding hours long waits at the polls.

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:24.429
For what’s to come, I can only trust god.

00:00:24.429 --> 00:00:29.800
We are tracking what could be the largest
election turnout in U.S. history.

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:30.800
Vote.

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:35.380
I made a plan to vote because I am not leaving
anything up to chance.

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:38.428
One of the most important elections of our
lifetime.

00:01:10.571 --> 00:01:11.830
Love it.

00:01:11.830 --> 00:01:16.505
Awesome thank you so much.

00:01:16.505 --> 00:01:17.720
It is currently 5:15 a.m.

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:22.350
I am walking across campus to meet a few other
students who are also going to be poll workers.

00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:24.440
Morning doctor, thanks for being with us.

00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:27.820
Every place in the country, people should
be using masks when they vote.

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:30.040
We have to do those things ourselves to change
the course.

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:35.820
It’s kind of paradoxical that although the
pandemic would make people more concerned

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:36.820
about coming here.

00:01:36.820 --> 00:01:43.140
But at the same time the government’s reaction
to the pandemic, eh, all of that instigated

00:01:43.140 --> 00:01:45.360
more fear that made people want to come and
vote.

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:46.860
You know the difference is mostly with the
masks.

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:52.159
You know and getting used to the mask and
getting used to people being around you.

00:01:52.159 --> 00:01:53.159
Some with mask, some without mask.

00:01:53.159 --> 00:01:55.350
The main thing is to get out and vote.

00:01:55.350 --> 00:02:00.990
Regardless we don’t let things stop us from
getting out to vote.

00:02:00.990 --> 00:02:04.750
Yes, wear the mask when you go voting.

00:02:04.750 --> 00:02:07.549
They made sure you had your mask on.

00:02:07.549 --> 00:02:09.399
It was safe to do so.

00:02:09.399 --> 00:02:13.930
Uh, what motivated you to come out and vote
in this election?

00:02:13.930 --> 00:02:19.069
Uh, I was just hoping to make America great
again.

00:02:19.069 --> 00:02:22.489
To keep it that way.

00:02:22.489 --> 00:02:25.670
Early voting started this morning and it runs
through the end of the month.

00:02:25.670 --> 00:02:28.060
Number of voters that are deciding to vote
early.

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:32.129
Record number of Americans taking advantage
of early voting.

00:02:32.129 --> 00:02:37.519
I just wanted to make sure I did my due diligence
and actually came in.

00:02:37.519 --> 00:02:42.989
So if I come here, I’ll stick my ballot
in the box and we’re good to go.

00:02:42.989 --> 00:02:48.659
The fact that people are waiting so patiently
is a good thing on one hand, but it’s also

00:02:48.659 --> 00:02:50.760
a reminder that it shouldn’t be like this.

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:56.849
I need you to not your mask and I don’t
need you to post it on facebook because that

00:02:56.849 --> 00:02:57.849
hashtag is doing absolutely nothing.

00:02:57.849 --> 00:02:59.069
We gotta vote like this.

00:02:59.069 --> 00:03:07.129
History in the making ladies and gentlemen.

00:03:07.129 --> 00:03:11.569
Some voters waited in line for close to three
hours.

00:03:11.569 --> 00:03:16.110
So after three train rides, and a car ride
I was finally able to successfully cast my

00:03:16.110 --> 00:03:17.370
ballot.

00:03:17.370 --> 00:03:19.900
All done.

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:24.200
Not too much social distancing, but everybody
had on a mask.

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:25.680
So, we’re all done.

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:30.549
It’s been a hell of a year for, from the
pandemic, from everything we went through.

00:03:30.549 --> 00:03:36.389
I’m a small business owner, so I’ve really
seen a lot of change, but Trump will bring

00:03:36.389 --> 00:03:37.389
it back.

00:03:37.389 --> 00:03:41.099
I’m worried about what’s going to come
after the election.

00:03:41.099 --> 00:03:43.090
What’s going to happen throughout the day.

00:03:43.090 --> 00:03:44.329
Is there going to be any kind of violence?

00:03:44.329 --> 00:03:52.059
Is there going to be any sort of initiative
to try to disregard the results or try to

00:03:52.059 --> 00:03:54.840
put doubt in the legitimacy of our elections.

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:57.230
That’s where my concern lies.

00:03:57.230 --> 00:04:01.290
Are mostly focused on mail-in ballots remaining.

00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:05.269
This is a tight race and there are any number
of ballots that have not been counted because

00:04:05.269 --> 00:04:06.430
of these delays.

00:04:06.430 --> 00:04:09.489
We were getting ready for a big celebration.

00:04:09.489 --> 00:04:12.370
Power can’t be taken or served.

00:04:12.370 --> 00:04:14.669
It flows from the people.

00:04:14.669 --> 00:04:20.400
Ok so the relief of voting is that you know
your votes in there, you’ve stood for something.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:22.019
And that’s what counts.

00:04:22.019 --> 00:04:23.019
Yes.

00:04:23.019 --> 00:04:28.690
That whether your party wins or loses, you’re
standing for what you believe in.

00:04:28.690 --> 00:04:29.690
Yes, yes.

00:04:29.690 --> 00:04:31.039
You are in the race.

00:04:31.039 --> 00:04:32.039
Yes.

00:04:32.039 --> 00:04:33.880
You’re in the race, but mostly for humanity,
equality and justice.

00:04:33.880 --> 00:04:34.880
That’s right.

00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:35.380
That’s right.

